<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuri al-Said</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuri al-Said was an Iraqi soldier and statesman who served as prime minister of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> many times between 1930 and 1958. A veteran of the Arab Revolt, he favoured close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and took Iraq into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact">Baghdad Pact</a> in 1955. He became prime minister of the Arab Federation in 1958 and was killed in the July revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuri-al-said.jpg" alt="Nuri al-Said" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouri_Al-Saeed,_1950s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
